PRACTICAL PYTHON
ORGANIZING CODE
Splitting Code into Reusable Functions
============================================================

1. INTRODUCTION

1.1 Why Organize Your Code?

As Python scripts grow, they become increasingly difficult to read, understand, and maintain.

Writing all the code in a single file can make a project complicated.

The solution is to organize your code by:
- Splitting functionality into reusable functions.
- Moving helper functions into separate Python files.
- Keeping the main script simple and readable.

This approach makes your project easier to maintain and expand.

1.2 Benefits of Organizing Code

1. Reusability:
   Write a function once and reuse it multiple times without rewriting the same logic.

2. Readability:
   Keep the main Python script simple, clean, and easy to understand.

3. Testability:
   Individual functions can be tested independently, making it easier to identify and fix errors.

