============================================================
7. KEY TAKEAWAYS
============================================================

1. Avoid putting all your code into one large Python file.

2. Create functions for reusable operations.

3. Keep helper functions in separate files when appropriate.

4. Use import statements to access functions from other modules.

5. Keep your main script clean and easy to understand.

6. Organize project files into meaningful folders.

7. Write functions that perform specific tasks.

IMPORTANT:
This is how real-world Python projects are commonly organized.

As your projects become larger, you can expand this structure by creating additional modules and packages.

